Subject: windows.ui.xaml: Frame navigation history, DispatcherTimer, AutomationProperties, Flyout and VisualTreeHelper

Frame now keeps a back and a forward stack of PageStackEntry objects (IFrame2.BackStack/ForwardStack,
IFrame2.Navigate with a transition, IFrame3.GoBack, GoBack/GoForward, CanGoBack/CanGoForward, BackStackDepth) and
navigates in WinUI's order: Navigating and the old page's OnNavigatingFrom (either may cancel), the new page, the
history, OnNavigatedFrom, the new content, Navigated, then the new page's OnNavigatedTo, each with the right
NavigationMode. Page implements IPageOverrides (the base versions do nothing), so apps' OnNavigatedTo now runs.
A page whose NavigationCacheMode is not Disabled is kept in its stack entry and shown again on Back/Forward.
A page that can't be created raises NavigationFailed. Transitions are kept, not played.

DispatcherTimer raises Tick from a thread timer on the thread that started it and keeps itself alive while it
runs. AutomationProperties (statics 1-9) are attached properties kept in the property store, so what an app sets
it reads back; nothing is exposed to UI Automation yet. Flyout shows its Content in a light-dismiss popup next to
its ShowAt target, placed by Placement. VisualTreeHelper walks our element tree (GetChild, GetChildrenCount,
GetParent, FindElementsInHostCoordinates by arranged bounds); GetOpenPopups lists none, as there is no Popup class.

Xbox Accessories needs all of these to build its LandingPage and its error dialogs. The IDL is generated from
Windows.winmd.

